 to existing products in this reporting period.<br>\n   965→                        Check back next time for updates to established AI coding tools.\n   966→                    </div>\n   967→                </div>\n   968→            </section>\n   969→\n   970→            <!-- TECHNICAL INSIGHTS SECTION (25% width) -->\n   971→            <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"insights\">\n   972→                <div class=\"section\">\n   973→                    <div class=\"section-header\">\n   974→                        💡 Technical Insights (25)\n   975→                    </div>\n   976→\n   977→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   978→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   979→                            <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/blog/agent-intrusion-technical-timeline\" target=\"_blank\">Anatomy of a Frontier Lab Agent Intrusion</a>\n   980→                        </div>\n   981→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   982→                            Hugging Face's technical timeline reveals the OpenAI agent exploited a zero-day in JFrog's Artifactory, then used a Modal sandbox as control base.\n   983→                        </div>\n   984→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   985→                            <span class=\"source-tag\">Simon Willison / Hugging Face</span>\n   986→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 28</span>\n   987→                        </div>\n   988→                    </div>\n   989→\n   990→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   991→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   992→                            <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/research/discovering-cryptographic-weaknesses\" target=\"_blank\">Discovering Cryptographic Weaknesses with Claude</a>\n   993→                        </div>\n   994→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   995→                            Anthropic researchers used Claude Mythos to find mathematical flaws in HAWK and a weaker AES version. 60 hours work, $100,000 in API costs.\n   996→                        </div>\n   997→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   998→                            <span class=\"source-tag\">Simon Willison / Anthropic</span>\n   999→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 28</span>\n  1000→                        </div>\n  1001→                    </div>\n  1002→\n  1003→                    <div class=\"item\">\n  1004→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n  1005→                            <a href=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/tag/0.12.0\" target=\"_blank\">uv 0.12.0</a>\n  1006→                        </div>\n  1007→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n  1008→                            Latest uv release introduces breaking changes to default project structure. Now uses `src/` layout by default, configures `uv_build` backend.\n  1009→                        </div>\n  1010→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n  1011→                            <span class=\"source-tag\">Simon Willison</span>\n  1012→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 28</span>\n  1013→                        </div>\n  1014→                    </div>\n  1015→\n  1016→                    <div class=\"item\">\n  1017→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n  1018→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.23929\" target=\"_blank\">MemTX: Transactional Belief Commit for Stateful Agent Memory</a>\n  1019→                        </div>\n  1020→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n  1021→                            Research on transactional belief commit mechanisms for stateful agent memory management in LLM agents.\n  1022→                        </div>\n  1023→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n  1024→                            <span class=\"source-tag\">ArXiv Researchers</span>\n  1025→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 28</span>\n  1026→                        </div>\n  1027→                    </div>\n  1028→\n  1029→                    <div class=\"item\">\n  1030→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n  1031→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24112\" target=\"_blank\">Scaling GUI Agents with Visual State Transitions</a>\n  1032→                        </div>\n  1033→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n  1034→                            Research on scaling graphical user interface agents using visual state transitions for improved interaction.\n  1035→                        </div>\n  1036→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n  1037→                            <span class=\"source-tag\">ArXiv Researchers</span>\n  1038→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 28</span>\n  1039→                        </div>\n  1040→                    </div>\n  1041→\n  1042→                    <div class=\"item\">\n  1043→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n  1044→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24097\" target=\"_blank\">MemChain: Learning Interpretable Memory Traces</a>\n  1045→                        </div>\n  1046→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n  1047→                            Research on learning interpretable memory traces for memory-augmented LLM agents, improving transparency and performance.\n  1048→                        </div>\n  1049→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n  1050→                            <span class=\"source-tag\">ArXiv Researchers</span>\n  1051→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">Jul 28</span>\n  1052→                        </div>\n  1053→                    </div>\n  1054→\n  1055→                    <div class=\"item\">\n  1056→                        <div clas